<h1>Heaven and Earth Qigong</h1>
<p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.15em;color:#5A9EAD;" class="reveal">Six movements. One complete, balanced practice you can keep for life.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:1.2em;" class="reveal"><a href="/why-qigong-training/" style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Why choose this training?</a></p>

<div class="shared-story reveal">
<p>Heaven and Earth Qigong is a stand-alone set of six movements, and one of the most rewarding practices Seb knows - the one he returns to constantly in his own training. Practised properly, it brings balance across the whole meridian system, settles the mind and leaves the body genuinely energised rather than merely stretched.</p>
</div>

<p class="reveal">"Practised properly" is the key phrase. The same six movements can be performed as nothing more than gentle exercise, and much of what is sold as Qigong today is exactly that: slowed-down aerobics wearing traditional clothing. The movements are one tool among several - a means, never the end. What makes this set Qigong is the internal work: a quiet, well-aligned body; breath that helps guide the Qi and settle the mind; intention (Yi) using the subtleties inside each movement to lead the Qi with accuracy; and listening awareness that gives you real, tangible feedback. Qi does not need to be visualised. It can be felt, and learning to feel it is central to this course.</p>

<p class="reveal">This course teaches the Five Elements version of Heaven and Earth, and it is suitable for any level of experience. The same external movements can also be practised as an Eight Extraordinary Meridians Qigong - an advanced, internally very different practice taught in the <a href="/online-courses/eight-extraordinary-meridians/">Eight Extraordinary Meridians course</a>.</p>

<h3 class="reveal">What You Will Learn</h3>
<ul class="features reveal">
<li>A quiet body and mind through Wuji stance - poor posture is noise, and noise destroys the focus that guides the Qi</li>
<li>Each of the six movements in turn, with the detail that makes them work</li>
<li>The complete set, with the Five Elements focus points that turn movement into Qigong</li>
<li>Breathing that supports both the Qi work and a calm, settled state of mind</li>
<li>Listening awareness: tangible perception of the Qi and of the changes your practice produces</li>
</ul>

<p class="reveal">The course is deliberately structured - foundations first, then each movement, then the complete practice - so you always have what you need at the moment you need it. By the end you will know not only the form but which Element each part of it addresses.</p>

